# Minecraft Server + Terraform Repository Instructions

## Repository Purpose
This repository contains two things:
1. A Paper 1.20.4 Minecraft server (server files, plugins, configuration)
2. Terraform infrastructure-as-code for provisioning and managing the server's cloud host on Google Cloud Platform (GCP)

## Structure
- `/server/` — Minecraft server root (Paper JAR, world data, plugins, server config)
- `/server/plugins/` — Bukkit/Paper plugin JARs
- `/terraform/` — GCP Terraform configuration (compute instances, networking, firewall rules, storage)

## Conventions
- Minecraft server version: Paper 1.20.4
- Cloud provider: Google Cloud Platform (GCP)
- Infrastructure managed entirely via Terraform; do not modify GCP resources manually
- Secrets (GCP credentials, RCON passwords, etc.) must never be committed — use `.gitignore` and environment variables or Secret Manager
- `start.sh` uses Aikar's JVM flags and should remain the canonical server start script

## Minecraft Server
- Default port: 25565
- EULA accepted: `/server/eula.txt`
- Plugins go in `/server/plugins/`

## Terraform
- All infrastructure changes must be applied via `terraform plan` / `terraform apply`
- Remote state should be stored in a GCS bucket (never commit `terraform.tfstate` locally)
